-- title:
--   Idempotents in the ideal (F,V) have ordinary image
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $B$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose coalgebra structure is cocommutative and which is finite and free as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module; write $D = \mathrm{CartierDual}(\mathbb{Z}/p, B)$ for the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear dual $\mathrm{Module.Dual}\,(\mathbb{Z}/p)\,B$ with its dual Hopf algebra structure, and for a bialgebra map $f$ let [`CartierDual.map`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDualMap.html#L102) $f$ denote the transposed bialgebra map of duals. Let $\varepsilon : B \to B$ be a bialgebra endomorphism with $\varepsilon \circ \varepsilon = \varepsilon$. Assume: for every bialgebra endomorphism $F_k$ of $B$ with $F_k x = x^p$ for all $x$, and every $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra endomorphism $F_D$ of $D$ with $F_D \psi = \psi^p$ for all $\psi$, there are bialgebra endomorphisms $a, b$ of $D$ such that the linear endomorphism underlying [`CartierDual.map`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDualMap.html#L102) $\varepsilon$ equals the convolution product of $F_D \circ a$ with $b \circ (\mathrm{CartierDual.map}\ F_k)$, the product being taken in the convolution monoid `WithConv` on $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear endomorphisms of $D$. Then there exist a commutative ring $C$ with a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, finite and free as a module, and bialgebra maps $q : B \to C$, $i : C \to B$ with $q$ surjective, $q \circ i = \mathrm{id}_C$ and $i \circ q = \varepsilon$, together with commutative rings $M$ (a Hopf algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, finite and free as a module) and $E$ (a Hopf algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$) and a bijective bialgebra map $\Theta : C \to M \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} E$ such that $E$ and $\mathrm{CartierDual}(\mathbb{Z}/p, M)$ are reduced.
--
--   In the language of finite commutative group schemes over $\mathbb{F}_p$, this says that an idempotent endomorphism whose Cartier transpose lies in the two-sided ideal generated by Frobenius and Verschiebung cuts out an ordinary direct factor: the image splits off as a quotient $C$ which decomposes as a tensor product of a group scheme with reduced dual (multiplicative type) and a reduced one (étale type), with no local-local part. It is used in the slope-principle arguments for $p$-divisible groups, and is cited by the statements about reductions satisfying a Frobenius–Verschiebung convolution identity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_exists_split_idempotent_bijective_tensorProduct_isReduced_cartierDual_of_cartierDualMap_eq_frobenius_conv_verschiebung.lean

